.el .ds Aq '
.TH fleetring-agent 1  FleetRing "FleetRing manual"
.SH NAME
fleetring\-agent \- Adds, lists, shows, renews, and removes agents\*(Aq identities
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfleetring agent\fR [\fB\-\-log\-format\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Adds, lists, shows, renews, and removes agents\*(Aq identities
.PP
An identity is a principal `agent\-<id>` with a certificate and a scoped token, kept in a directory per agent (ADR\-0043, point 8). In dev mode, `fleetring mcp \-\-agent <id>` adds one by itself. A delegated agent, such as `42.c7`, holds only a narrower token, which its parent asks the control plane for with `agent delegate`, and connects with its root\*(Aqs certificate (ADR\-0047). Trusted local development: agents running as the same user can read each other\*(Aqs credentials.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-format\fR \fI<LOG_FORMAT>\fR
Writes log lines as `text` or `json`

Overrides `FLEETRING_LOG_FORMAT` and the configuration file\*(Aqs `[log] format`.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Prints the result and errors only

No progress, notes, warnings or override warnings. A command with no result then prints nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour log lines and the picker

`auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`; `always` and `never` do as they say.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: On a terminal, unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`
.IP \(bu 2
always: Always, even into a pipe or a file
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
fleetring\-agent\-add(1)
Mints an agent\*(Aqs identity: a certificate and a scoped token
.TP
fleetring\-agent\-delegate(1)
Asks the control plane for a delegated agent\*(Aqs token, as its parent
.TP
fleetring\-agent\-list(1)
Lists the context\*(Aqs agents, with their scopes and expiries
.TP
fleetring\-agent\-show(1)
Shows one agent: its principal, scopes, expiries, files, and MCP command
.TP
fleetring\-agent\-renew(1)
Reissues an agent\*(Aqs certificate and token now, and revokes the old token
.TP
fleetring\-agent\-remove(1)
Revokes an agent and every agent below it, and deletes its directory
